From: Samaksh Kamboj <samakshk4@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] NTCamera: offer 720p/480p video quality options

The HAL exposes 720p/480p recording sizes (Aperture uses them) and the
filter logic already emits quality IDs 5/4 when supported; only the
settings arrays lack the entries. Recording fps still comes from the
separate 30/60 fps preference.

The same preference points camera:icons at @array/video_quality_icons,
which IconListPreference.filterUnsupported() indexes in parallel with
entryValues; leaving it at two items makes the app throw
ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException (length=2; index=2) as soon as a third
quality is supported. Extend it too (the app already reuses
ic_video_quality_high in video_timelapse_icons).

---
--- a/res/values/arrays.xml
+++ b/res/values/arrays.xml
@@ -3019,10 +3019,14 @@
     <string-array name="pref_video_quality_entries">
         <item>@string/pref_video_quality_entry_fine</item>
         <item>@string/pref_video_quality_entry_4k</item>
+        <item>@string/pref_video_quality_entry_high</item>
+        <item>@string/pref_video_quality_entry_medium</item>
     </string-array>
     <string-array name="pref_video_quality_entryvalues">
         <item>6</item>
         <item>8</item>
+        <item>5</item>
+        <item>4</item>
     </string-array>
     <string-array name="pref_video_record_red_light_entries">
         <item>@string/pref_video_record_red_light_entry_off</item>
@@ -3308,6 +3312,8 @@
     <array name="video_quality_icons">
         <item>@drawable/ic_video_quality_fine</item>
         <item>@drawable/ic_video_quality_4k</item>
+        <item>@drawable/ic_video_quality_high</item>
+        <item>@drawable/ic_video_quality_high</item>
     </array>
     <array name="video_stabilization_icons">
         <item>@drawable/ic_video_stabilization_off</item>
